ed-state-node1","cmd-282475163c074691","cmd-e4832e7c56214e46"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after execution. The implementation used the platform's installed OpenSSH and standard shell utilities, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Chronological review found no unnecessary state-changing experiments: account/key creation, receiver and SSH configuration, test submissions, marker setup, and restarts all had clear task or evidence roles. One executor-caused residue remained on node2: /tmp/restriction-test.ndjson, created for the restriction test and not cleaned afterward. No failed services, added listeners, or package damage were observed. Both nodes completed the restart protocol with healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, and end-to-end ingestion.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f3973929a7841e5","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","cmd-c074a2923e2f4813","cmd-10e4aadee481489a","cmd-833113e87c5f4bbe","cmd-282475163c074691","cmd-581c066b670b409c","cmd-b9d39d0d275f45e9","cmd-97d42779055e4ec0","cmd-fd025b012dfc45cd","cmd-e4832e7c56214e46","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The dedicated key successfully performs exact-byte ingestion while arbitrary command execution and forwarding are blocked; seeded data, OS release, kernel, and functionality survive verified restarts of both nodes. The only hygiene defect is one abandoned temporary restriction-test file on node2.","limitations":["No explicit interactive shell/PTY attempt was captured; shell denial is supported by the directly demonstrated forced-command boundary and effective PermitTTY=no policy.","Lifecycle file and socket inventories are bounded rather than exhaustive, though they directly identify the lone test-file residue and show no failed services, unexpected listeners, or package inconsistency."]}
